    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Diagnostic criteria for lung involvement by Erdheim&ndash;Chester disease (ECD) {10789787; 9888700; 20662053; 24850756}</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Neval Ozkaya",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"background: #DAEEF3; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>For first-time diagnosis of ECD (with pulmonary presentation):</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>Essential:</em></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Histiocytic infiltrate with characteristic lymphangitic distribution<sup>a</sup></p>\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Non-Langerhans cell phenotype</p>\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Characteristic chest CT findings</p>\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Additional systemic findings<sup>b</sup></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>Desirable:</em></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Corroborating genetic alteration</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>When there is already a well-established diagnosis of ECD involving another site<sup>b</sup>:</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>Essential<sup>c</sup>:</em></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Characteristic chest CT findings</p>\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Exclusion of other possible etiologies of interstitial lung disease</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>Desirable:</em></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Histiocytic infiltrate with characteristic lymphangitic distribution<sup>a</sup></p>\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Non-Langerhans cell phenotype</p>\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Corroborating genetic alteration</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Transbronchial lung biopsies are often unhelpful in showing the characteristic distribution, but wedge biopsies can exhibit diagnostic features.</p>\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>b</sup>The diagnosis of ECD should be made by identifying distinctive histopathological findings from any site in the appropriate clinical and radiological context (see Table &lt;&lt;#14216&gt;&gt;).</p>\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>c</sup>Diagnosis of pulmonary ECD is highly likely under these circumstances, although a definitive diagnosis always requires histopathological evaluation.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 37782,
    "bookid": 35,
    "chapterId": 107,
    "fileId": 14216,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Common sites of involvement by Erdheim&ndash;Chester disease</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Neval Ozkaya",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border: none; \" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong style=\"\">Site</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 578.9pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"772\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong style=\"\">Manifestations</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">Bones (80&ndash;95%)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 578.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"772\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Bilateral symmetrical long bone involvement at the metadiaphysis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">Retroperitoneum (55&ndash;65%)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 578.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"772\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Perinephric infiltration (&ldquo;hairy kidneys&rdquo;)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">Vasculature (50&ndash;80%)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 578.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"772\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Periaortic infiltration of the entire thoracoabdominal aorta (&ldquo;coated aorta&rdquo;), supra-aortic trunks, and coronary arteries</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">Heart (40&ndash;70%)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 578.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"772\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Right atrial pseudotumour; valvular infiltration; pericardial infiltration and effusion</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">Endocrine system (40&ndash;70%)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 578.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"772\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Diabetes insipidus; anterior pituitary dysfunction; testicular insufficiency; adrenal infiltration</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">Nervous system (40%)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 578.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"772\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Brainstem/cerebellum masses; cerebral white matter enhancement; dural and pituitary stalk thickening</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">Respiratory tract (30&ndash;55%)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 578.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"772\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Mediastinal infiltration; pleural, septal, and maxillary sinus thickening</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">Orbits (30%)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 578.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"772\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Orbital masses</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">Skin (25&ndash;30%)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 578.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"772\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Xanthelasma-like lesions around the eyes, face, neck, and inguinal folds</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  }
]